+### Tenka (new girl, Meshy API rig + a separate coilgun GLB)
+
+Tenka is built by the same tool with a per-figure profile (`tools/meshy/lib/profiles.py`;
+`--profile hikari` is the default and rebuilds Hikari exactly as before):
+
+```
+python3 tools/meshy/build_meshy_chibi.py --profile tenka --source <tenka rigged GLB> --clips <Meshy-library animated GLB>
+python3 tools/meshy/build_meshy_prop.py --source <coilgun GLB> --id tenka-coilgun --unit tenka
+```
+
+- source: a Meshy API rig (24 bones `Hips … RightToeBase`, Armature scale 0.01, a ~0.9 m figure).
+  `normalize` applies the armature scale, scales her to the tool's 1.7 m working height (the face
+  window, bake cage and eye windows are tuned there) and centres her; the bones are renamed to the
+  readable set and get an unweighted floor `root`. Bake sources are found by shader-socket links
+  (her images are not named like Hikari's). Battle height 1.224, like Hikari.
+- eyes: amber iris and blue-violet hair predicates, a tighter search window (her lashes sit close to
+  the bangs' strand outlines), mirrored boxes. `extras.eyes.hairGuard` = `{ hue: [180, 260], sat 0.6,
+  val 0.12 }` (linear-RGB HSV) keeps her blue bangs and teal streaks as painted when the eyes close
+  (`figurine.js` `figGuard`; a figure without it keeps Hikari's pink rule).
+- clips (`lib/clips_tenka.py`): `idle` 1.5 s, `walk` 0.97 s (library), `attack_rifle` 0.6 s (aimed by
+  0.07 s, recoil kick and two muzzle flips, so the shot reads even when `attackFx` restarts the clip
+  every 0.45 s), `cheer` 1.2 s (coilgun raised), `hurt` 0.4 s; every clip has a 14° chin-up
+  (spine 3°, neck 6°, head 5°) so her eyes clear the bangs at 48°. `extras.weaponKind` is `rifle`.
+- coilgun: its own GLB (`tenka-coilgun.glb`, 3k tris, base 512² + metal/roughness 256², stored at
+  half size like the figures). The figure carries an empty socket node `prop_coilgun` under
+  `hand_R` (it holds the grip frame and scale) and lists the file in `extras.props` (and the
+  manifest entry's `props`). `glbChibi.js` loads each prop once, gives it the figurine material, a
+  texture-tinted outline and the selection highlight, and hangs it under the socket of every
+  instance, so the clips move it with her hand.
+
 ## Judging quality
 
